<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25161" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jactātor</span></b> , ōris,
			m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>one who makes an ostentatious display of himself, a boaster,
				braggart</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rerum a se gestarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 11, 1, 17</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">civilitatis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Claud. 35</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 6, 837</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 18,
				4, 1</span></i>.—<b>Poet.</b>, with <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ille sub hiberno somnos educere caelo Jactator,</span>”
				<i>he boasts</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					11, 403</span></i>
			.</div>
